  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The foundational QMS standard for any organisation manufacturing medical devices — hardware, SaMD, or AI/ML systems. Harmonised with EU MDR/IVDR and recognised across MDSAP participating jurisdictions (EU, Canada, Australia, Japan, Brazil). Compliance is a prerequisite for CE marking and market access in most regulated markets. Applies to the full device lifecycle including design, development, and post-market surveillance. Note: this is a paid ISO standard (approx. CHF 158); unlike open interoperability standards such as FHIR or DICOM it is not freely available. Adopt means compliance is mandatory for any team building regulated medical device software — not that the standard is open access.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-05",
